ong><p>Think carefully about the boundaries between systems.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Always learning</strong><p>Explore ideas, document lessons, and keep improving.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section id="notes" class="section wrap notes"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow dark">03 / FIELD NOTES</div><h2>Thinking out loud<span class="period">.</span></h2></div><p>Notes on the tools and ideas behind dependable automation software.</p></div><a class="note-row" href="/blog/designing-for-connection/"><span>01 / CONNECTIVITY</span><div><h3>Designing for a connection that can fail</h3><p>Some practical questions for a TCP/IP client.</p></div><span class="note-arrow">↗</span></a><a class="note-row" href="/blog/wpf-mvvm/"><span>02 / DESKTOP</span><div><h3>Why separate the view from the work?</h3><p>A short introduction to WPF and MVVM.</p></div><span class="note-arrow">↗</span></a><a class="note-row" href="/blog/from-signals-to-context/"><span>03 / SYSTEMS</span><div><h3>From equipment signals to useful context</h3><p>Thinking about the journey from PLC to MES.</p></div><span class="note-arrow">↗</span></a></section><section class="contact wrap"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / GET IN TOUCH</div><h2>Let's build something<br/><em>that works.</em></h2><p>Interested in industrial software, connectivity, or a thoughtful technical conversation?</p></div><a class="button light" href="https://github.com/EvanHan-dev">Find me on GitHub <span>↗</span></a></section></Base>

